.next/
# Generated and re-generated by Next.js on every `next dev` / `next build`, and its contents
# differ between the two (`.next/dev/types/` vs `.next/types/`), so a tracked copy is dirty
# after whichever command ran last. Next 16's own docs are explicit: "next-env.d.ts is managed
# by Next.js. Its contents are an implementation detail and may change over time. Add it to
# .gitignore. If your project already tracks the file, remove it from Git."
# -- node_modules/next/dist/docs/01-app/03-api-reference/05-config/02-typescript.md
next-env.d.ts
.vercel
.claude/
*.tsbuildinfo
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/
playwright/.cache/
